## Test Smell Audit — Academic 19-Smell Catalog (testsmells.org)

**Target:** `DataAccess.IntegrationTests/UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`  
**Framework:** MSTest 4.1 / .NET 10  
**Integration calibration applied:** Class is annotated `[TestCategory("Integration")]`

---

### Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High     | 2           | 2              |
| Medium   | 2           | 2              |
| Low      | 0           | 0              |
| **Total**| **4**       | **4**          |

---

### Findings by Severity

#### 🔴 HIGH — Conditional Test Logic

**Test:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (line 95)  
**Problem:** `if`/`else` branch means one assertion path *never executes* per run — hidden testing gap.

```csharp
// SMELL: different assertions run depending on runtime type
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

**Fix:** Split into two focused tests, or use a deterministic setup so the type is known:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_WhenStandard_ReturnsCorrectName()
{
    var user = new User("eve@example.com", "Eve");
    _repository.Insert(user);
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");
    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_WhenPremium_HasPositiveDiscount()
{
    var user = new PremiumUser("eve@example.com", "Eve", discountRate: 0.1m);
    _repository.Insert(user);
    var loaded = (PremiumUser)_repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com")!;
    Assert.IsTrue(loaded.DiscountRate > 0);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** One branch is never validated in CI; a regression hides silently.

---

#### 🔴 HIGH — Assertion-Free Test (Unknown Test)

**Test:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (line 113)  
**Problem:** No assertion — test passes even if inserts silently fail or corrupt data.

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }
    // No assertion — false confidence
}
```

**Fix:** Assert the observable outcome:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }

    var all = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(100, all.Count);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** 100 % false-pass rate — the test cannot detect any bug.

---

#### 🟡 MEDIUM — Sleepy Test *(downgraded from High; integration calibration applied)*

**Test:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 82)  
**Problem:** `Thread.Sleep(3000)` adds 3 s of wall-clock time and is non-deterministic under load.

```csharp
Thread.Sleep(3000);
Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id));
```

**Fix:** Poll with a timeout or use an async wait handle:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public async Task NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay()
{
    var user = new User("dave@example.com", "Dave");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    // Poll with back-off instead of a fixed sleep
    var sent = await WaitUntilAsync(
        () => _repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id),
        timeout: TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5));

    Assert.IsTrue(sent, "Notification was not sent within timeout.");
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Flaky failures in CI; 3 s per run accumulates across the suite.

---

#### 🟡 MEDIUM — Assertion Roulette

**Test:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (line 28)  
**Problem:** 4 assertions with no message parameters — a failure reports only "Assert.AreEqual failed" with no context on *which* property was wrong.

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
```

**Fix:** Add discriminating messages:

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should round-trip");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should round-trip");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Id should be assigned by the database");
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Slower triage — developers must re-run or read source to locate the failure.

---

### Smell-Free Patterns ✅

The remaining **4 tests** are well-structured:

| Test | Why it's good |
|------|--------------|
| `UpdateUser_ModifiesExistingRecord` | Clear arrange/act/assert, focused scope |
| `DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase` | Single behavior, negative assertion is appropriate |
| `ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted` | Count is self-documenting (3 inserts → expect 3) |
| `InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity` | Proper async/await, focused concurrency check |

The `[TestInitialize]` fixture is lean and used by every test — no General Fixture smell. The in-memory SQLite connection is hermetic, so no Mystery Guest despite being an integration suite.

---

### Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Fix Effort | Impact |
|----------|-------|-----------|--------|
| 1 | Assertion-Free Test | ~2 min | Eliminates a test that *cannot* catch bugs |
| 2 | Conditional Test Logic | ~5 min | Ensures both type paths are validated every run |
| 3 | Sleepy Test | ~10 min | Removes 3 s flakiness + speeds suite |
| 4 | Assertion Roulette | ~3 min | Improves failure diagnostics |

**Bottom line:** 4 of 8 tests are clean. The two High-severity smells (#1 and #2) should be fixed immediately — one test *cannot detect any bug*, and another has an assertion gap that may *never* be exercised. The Medium findings are quality-of-life improvements that reduce flakiness and triage time.
